<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antonio Nariño</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1765">1765</a>–<a href="/years/1823">1823</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antonio Nariño was a New Granadan revolutionary who translated and printed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/declaration-of-the-rights-of-man-and-of-the-citizen">Declaration of the Rights of Man</a> in 1794 and was imprisoned for it. He became president of the Free and Independent State of Cundinamarca in 1811 and led its centralist cause against the federalist United Provinces. He was captured by royalists in 1814 and later served in independent Colombia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antonio-narino.jpg" alt="Antonio Nariño" width="320" height="466" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ricardo Acevedo Bernal · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nari%C3%B1o_by_Acevedo_Bernal.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
